  "name": null,
  "problem": "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=6{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=-5{c}_{2}+9{c}_{3}-4{c}_{1}.$",
